<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal Jan-May insurance premiums drop yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Portugal Jan-May insurance premiums drop yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese insurance premiums totalled 307.547 billion escudos in the period from January to May, 3.3 percent less than in the same period last year, the Portuguese Association of Insurers (APS) said.</p>
<p>Life insurance premiums fell to 117.475 billion escudos from January to May, 11.9 percent less than from January to May 1996.</p>
<p>Within this category, the volume of retirement savings plans rose 14.8 percent to 14.322 billion escudos from January to May this year, compared with the same period last year.</p>
<p>	    INSURANCE PREMIUMS (billion escudos)</p>
<p>				Jan-May97	Jan-May96	Variation</p>
<p>Life			  117.475	  133.399	 -11.9 pct</p>
<p>  incl. RSPs		 14.322	   12.472	  14.8 pct</p>
<p>Accidents and sickness   55.430	   52.561	   5.5 pct</p>
<p>Fires, property damages  27.726	   26.474	   4.7 pct</p>
<p>Automobile insurance     97.090	   96.032	   1.1 pct</p>
<p>     TOTAL NON-LIFE     190.072	  184.759	   2.9 pct</p>
<p>     TOTAL OVERALL	307.547	  318.159	  -3.3 pct</p>
<p>Note:  The above figures are taken from insurers representing between 88 and 92 percent of the Portuguese insurance market.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
